<http://data.silknow.org/object/6a64d191-f936-305d-a4b1-b7a03ba20624>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Intended for use in embellishments for textiles."@en , "Textile, skeins, gold-wrapped thread, India, ca. 1855-1879"@en , "Bundle of skeins of gold-wrapped thread, joined, with 'India Office' label."@en , "[03/10/2015-10/01/2016]\nSILVER AND GOLD\n\nFor lavish decoration, embroiderers use thin strips of silver or gilded silver (zari), sequins and metal foil, often with tiny pearls. Yarn made of silk thread wrapped with silver (or gilded silver) can be woven or used for embroidery. Metal strips interwoven with silk produce luxurious shiny fabric or ribbon (gota) which can be applied onto cloth.\n\nSilver weave\nCotton warp and silver weft\nMurshidabad, West Bengal, about 1850\nV&A: 0708 (IS)\n\nGolden weave\nGilded silver warp and silk weft\nHyderabad, Andhra Pradesh/Telangana, about 1855\nV&A: 0695 (IS)\n\nPanel with mankolam (paisley) pattern\nSilk, metal-wrapped thread, sequins, pearls, silver strips\nTriplicane, Chennai, Tamil Nadu, 1855–79\nV&A: 6502 (IS)\n\nSilver and gilded silver embellishments\nHyderabad, Andhra Pradesh/Telangana, and Ahmedabad, Gujarat, about 1855\nV&A: 6293; 6345; 6346; 6354; 05954:1 to 3; 05939:1, 2 (IS) [03/10/2015-10/01/2016]"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/9ba88cfe-2179-34f7-9954-eef873c4368d> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Intended for use in embellishments for textiles."@en , "Bundle of skeins of gold-wrapped thread, joined, with 'India Office' label."@en , "[03/10/2015-10/01/2016]\nSILVER AND GOLD\n\nFor lavish decoration, embroiderers use thin strips of silver or gilded silver (zari), sequins and metal foil, often with tiny pearls. Yarn made of silk thread wrapped with silver (or gilded silver) can be woven or used for embroidery. Metal strips interwoven with silk produce luxurious shiny fabric or ribbon (gota) which can be applied onto cloth.\n\nSilver weave\nCotton warp and silver weft\nMurshidabad, West Bengal, about 1850\nV&A: 0708 (IS)\n\nGolden weave\nGilded silver warp and silk weft\nHyderabad, Andhra Pradesh/Telangana, about 1855\nV&A: 0695 (IS)\n\nPanel with mankolam (paisley) pattern\nSilk, metal-wrapped thread, sequins, pearls, silver strips\nTriplicane, Chennai, Tamil Nadu, 1855–79\nV&A: 6502 (IS)\n\nSilver and gilded silver embellishments\nHyderabad, Andhra Pradesh/Telangana, and Ahmedabad, Gujarat, about 1855\nV&A: 6293; 6345; 6346; 6354; 05954:1 to 3; 05939:1, 2 (IS) [03/10/2015-10/01/2016]"@en , "Textile, skeins, gold-wrapped thread, India, ca. 1855-1879"@en ;
